Standard Operating Procedure
Check and Terminate a Hung Application – Windows

Document Owner:
IT Support
Platform:
Windows 10 / 11

Effective Date:
31-Jul-2026
Review Cycle:
Annual

1. Purpose

This procedure describes the standard steps to verify that an application is running and to forcibly
terminate it when it has stopped responding (hung).

2. Scope

Applies to IT support staff and end users troubleshooting unresponsive desktop applications on Windows
systems.

3. Procedure

Step 1: Verify the application is running

Open Command Prompt and run the command below, replacing ApplicationName with the actual
process name.

tasklist | findstr "ApplicationName"

Step 2: Terminate the application

Once confirmed, force-terminate the process using the command below.

taskkill /F /IM ApplicationName.exe

4. Notes

The /F flag forces immediate termination and skips cleanup, so any unsaved data in the application may
be lost.

